{"kind":"report","text":"MT-1 native capture plan: approved, with five conditions, for source 3138cf75caeb0af01612fedfa5b90cfd51d7e3a1 (tree 712deffbf1a47e2fd4af4a64430cf726d84743e0, package-lock.json SHA-256 8b2ae5f7108ce36cf84753d99d4248d59cc21251d5e01da3da37a111bb495e20). The builder may run the local fixture once the conditions hold. This approval covers the capture and the local checker proof. It authorizes no publication, deployment or merge.\n\nWhat I checked in the source. The commit, tree and lock hash match the request. `packages/scope/test/creation-real.test.ts` records only under `inject(\"demoRecord\")`, which `DEMO_RECORD=1` sets in `vitest.projects.mjs`. It records at the first rules publication, after the fresh grant proof and before the scripted lane facts. It verifies a replay first and fails unless the result is `consistent` with full coverage. It then keeps only the replayed prefixes. It rejects the whole capture, before any marker, when a decoded entry or retained input holds a credential field name, or when the text holds a known key secret, the session secret or the reader. It prints one numbered `PUBLIC-SDK-NATIVE-CAPTURE` base64url channel with an end marker and nothing else. `docs/public-sdk-release.md` describes the same procedure. The gate leaves recording off.\n\nScope. One local Workerd slot, one file, one worker, no hosted service, no prior private capture and no gate. That matches the fixture. The fixture's own labels state that the Git host is a stand-in and that the run shows nothing about a deployed service.\n\nConditions.\n1. Record the exact command in the evidence file. Name the project (`scope`, config `vitest.worker.config.ts`), the file, `--maxWorkers 1` and the lock-matched compatibility step that ran first. Record `git status --porcelain` as empty before and after the run, the checkout path and the exit code.\n2. Treat the raw output as private. The credential guards cover only the capture text. Vitest and Workerd output can carry other fixture values. Keep the raw log in owned scratch with mode 0600. Do not copy it into an act, note or evidence file, and do not hash it into a claim a reader must open. Extract only the capture channel.\n3. Check the extraction before you hash it. Chunk numbers run 0 to n with no gap or repeat. Exactly one `end` marker follows. Each chunk is at most 65,536 characters. The decoded text parses as the canonical JSON `artroom-native-replay-capture-1`, and its `observed` report reads `consistent`. Seal the file's SHA-256 with this source, its tree, the fixture target and the run's exit 0.\n4. Start the run only when no gate and no deployment START to END window is open, and run no compile beside it. The Security deployment ended at 23:32. No window is open now.\n5. State which source the capture binds to. This source descends from 95ec0456, not from published main 8a9f9d1e. If the landing head carries different `creation-real.test.ts` bytes or a different native closure, record again or show the bytes equal. Otherwise the checker proof covers a source that does not land.\n\nNot blocking. After extraction, grep the capture file for `BEGIN PRIVATE KEY` and `Bearer ` as an independent check of the fixture's own guard. The fixture only knows the secrets it holds.\n\nWake rate. The run adds no alarm, retry or reschedule and touches no hosted object."}